# ============================================================================
# Monorepo build-context excludes. BOTH product stacks now build with
# context = repo root (the cargo workspace lives here), so this single file is
# shared by the hunter and forge image builds. Patterns
# are recursive (**/) because each product's tree is one level down.
# ============================================================================

# --- Rust build output (rebuilt inside the image) ---
**/target/
**/target-check/

# --- Node deps & build output (reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image) ---
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/

# --- VCS / migration backup / archives / editor noise ---
.git/
_monorepo-backup/
*.7z
*.zip
*.rar
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log

# --- Secrets — never copy into an image (runtime env arrives via compose env_file) ---
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/keystore/
**/wallet-backups/
**/*.enc
*.ppk
aws-ec2-key.pem
.mcp.json
# NOTE: nginx/tls/*.pem is deliberately NOT excluded — the frontend image COPYs
# the self-signed cert/key. The forge keystores / *.enc above are the secret set.

# --- Parquet lake / local data (never part of an image build) ---
**/.lake/
**/*.parquet
**/lake-data/
# Local research scratch + the runtime strategy event log (a named volume in
# compose, never baked into an image). Both churn constantly, and anything that
# churns inside the build context invalidates the source COPY layer and re-runs
# the cargo build for a change no crate can see.
**/_local/
**/event_log/
# Root-level scratch dumps (fp.json, trades.json, resp*.json, tr_*/ms_*.json,
# backup.dump). Patterns without **/ match the CONTEXT ROOT only, so the
# frontends' package.json / tsconfig.json are untouched.
*.json
*.dump

# --- Docs / plans (not needed to build; keep a docs edit from busting the
#     builder's source-copy layer and forcing a recompile) ---
**/*.md
**/@plans/
**/@arch/
**/docs/
